detection.description:
The main meter's raw per-phase readings. Active power per phase is what matters most; power factor, current and voltage refine the signatures where the meter publishes them. Every field is optional; a single-phase meter uses the A fields only.

Meters below this one need no setting up: the devices on your Energy dashboard are used automatically, nesting and all.

{found}

grid.description:
Where the site meets the utility, per phase. This is a different ROLE from the page above, not a different meter: the same inverter usually publishes both sides, and this page prefers the input, grid and mains readings that the other one pushes away.

It is here to complete the load signal. Where the inverter feeds the loads in parallel with the grid, the meter carries the house minus what the inverter makes, so neither reading alone is what the house draws and their sum is. Behind a transfer switch, or off grid, everything already comes through the inverter and adding the grid would count the pass-through twice.

